{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.even_tower_continuant_harmonics","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.even_tower_continuant_harmonics","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_recurrence"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.boson_tower_is_uniformly_harmonic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.boson_tower_is_uniformly_harmonic","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/even_tower_continuant_harmonics.lean#L189-L202","doc":"**Boson-tower harmonic summary.** All three electroweak carriers are\nharmonics of the fundamental Hopf continuant `b₂`, and `H`'s\ncoefficient additionally factors through `W`'s. Contrast the fermion\ntower, whose prime windings `3,5,7` are mutually non-divisible\n(the fermion generation-exclusion result, PR #4456): the boson\ntower is uniformly non-generational. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.b4_dvd_b8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.b4_dvd_b8","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/even_tower_continuant_harmonics.lean#L181-L187","doc":"**`H`'s continuant factors through `W`'s**: `b₄ ∣ b₈` with cofactor\n`X⁴ + 4X² + 2` (`b₈ = b₄·(X⁴ + 4X² + 2)`), the internal harmonic\n`T(2,8) = (T(2,4))²`-type factorisation on the normal-form data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.b2_dvd_b8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.b2_dvd_b8","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/even_tower_continuant_harmonics.lean#L175-L179","doc":"**`H ↔ T(2,8)` is a `b₂`-harmonic**: `b₈ = b₂·(X⁶ + 6X⁴ + 10X² + 4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.b2_dvd_b6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.b2_dvd_b6","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/even_tower_continuant_harmonics.lean#L170-L173","doc":"**`Z ↔ T(2,6)` is a `b₂`-harmonic**: `b₆ = b₂·(X⁴ + 4X² + 3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.b2_dvd_b4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.b2_dvd_b4","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/even_tower_continuant_harmonics.lean#L165-L168","doc":"**`W ↔ T(2,4)` is a `b₂`-harmonic**: `b₄ = b₂·(X² + 2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.morganVoyceB_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.morganVoyceB_eight","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/even_tower_continuant_harmonics.lean#L160-L163","doc":"`b₈ = X⁷ + 6X⁵ + 10X³ + 4X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.morganVoyceB_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.morganVoyceB_six","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/even_tower_continuant_harmonics.lean#L156-L158","doc":"`b₆ = X⁵ + 4X³ + 3X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.morganVoyceB_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.morganVoyceB_four","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/even_tower_continuant_harmonics.lean#L152-L154","doc":"`b₄ = X³ + 2X = X·(X² + 2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.morganVoyceB_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.morganVoyceB_two","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/even_tower_continuant_harmonics.lean#L148-L150","doc":"`b₂ = X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.b2_dvd_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.b2_dvd_even","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/even_tower_continuant_harmonics.lean#L135-L144","doc":"**Every even winding is a harmonic of the fundamental Hopf continuant\n`b₂`.** `b₂ ∣ b_{2k}` for all `k`: the entire boson (even-winding)\ntower descends from the single fundamental `b₂ = X`. This is the\nboson-side statement dual to the fermion generation-exclusion:\nthere is no even \"prime generation\" — every even winding factors\nthrough `b₂`, matching the non-generational gauge/link character of\nbosons (`boson_iff_even`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.morganVoyceB_dvd_of_dvd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.morganVoyceB_dvd_of_dvd","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/even_tower_continuant_harmonics.lean#L124-L131","doc":"**Strong divisibility of the Morgan–Voyce continuant.**\n`a ∣ n ⇒ b_a ∣ b_n` — the general theorem behind the fermion\ngeneration-exclusion instances and the boson harmonic tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.morganVoyceB_dvd_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.morganVoyceB_dvd_mul","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/even_tower_continuant_harmonics.lean#L108-L122","doc":"`b_n ∣ b_{n·k}`: the continuant coefficient of every multiple winding\nis divisible by that of the base winding. Proved by induction on `k`\nfrom the addition formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.morganVoyceB_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.morganVoyceB_add","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/even_tower_continuant_harmonics.lean#L77-L104","doc":"**Addition formula** for the Morgan–Voyce continuant `b_n`:\n`b_{m+n+1} = b_{m+1}·b_{n+1} + b_m·b_n`.\n\nDerived by two-step induction on `m` from\n`morganVoyceB_recurrence`; it is the polynomial Fibonacci addition\nlaw specialised to `b₁ = 1`, `b₂ = X`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}